              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB","AD","DB"] },
            { text: "is also that by which the sum of the squares on {AD} and {DB}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AD","DB"] },
            { text: "differs from the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"] },
            { text: "while twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB} exceeds twice the rectangle {AD} by {DB} by a rational area,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB","AD","DB"] },
            { text: "therefore the sum of the squares on {AD} and {DB} also exceeds the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AD","DB","AC","CB"] },
            { text: "by a rational area, though they are medial, which is impossible.",
              visible: ALL,
              justifications: [{ claim: "a medial area does not exceed a medial area by a rational area", ref: "X.26" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the side of a rational plus a medial area is not divided at different points,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["C","D"] },
